{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'ls -la; find /work -name AGENTS.md -o -name QRYPT-ISOLATED.txt; cat /work/QRYPT-ISOLATED.txt; curl -fsSL https://qrypt-quickstart.pages.dev/llms.txt'","aggregated_output":"total 12\ndrwx------ 2 agent agent 4096 Oct 15 17:30 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 root  root  4096 Oct 15 17:30 ..\n-r--r--r-- 1 agent agent  267 Oct 15 17:30 QRYPT-ISOLATED.txt\n/work/QRYPT-ISOLATED.txt\nQrypt Isolated Setup. You have NO QRYPT_API_KEY in this container — that is intentional.\nImplement the example from https://qrypt-quickstart.pages.dev/llms.txt and run mock tests.\nTell the human to run on the host: agent-sandbox/verify.sh --env <their-secret-path>\n# Qrypt quantum entropy quickstart (for AI agents)\n> Get an AES-256-GCM key from Qrypt quantum entropy. Plain HTTPS; no SDK exists for this API. Do not invent one.\n\n## Choose a mode\n- **Quick Setup (default, no Docker):** follow the rules below. The human creates `.env`; you never read it. Behavioral safeguards only — not isolation.\n- **Isolated Setup (Docker):** if `QRYPT-ISOLATED.txt` exists or the human said they are using `agent-sandbox/run.sh`, you have NO token. Implement the example, run mock tests, then tell the human to run `agent-sandbox/verify.sh --env <their-secret-path>` on the host. Do not ask for the token. Do not try to read any `.env`.\n\n## FIRST: secrets\n- NEVER ask the human to paste QRYPT_API_KEY into chat, a prompt, CLI args or source code.\n- NEVER read, print, cat, head, sed, less, or dump `.env` or environment variables. NEVER enable verbose HTTP logging of Authorization headers.\n- To check a `.env` exists without reading it: `test -f .env && echo set` (Quick Setup only). If that fails with Permission denied, you are misconfigured — stop and tell the human to use Isolated Setup.\n- If you read .env or any credential by accident, stop and tell the human so they can rotate it.\n- Keep the generated key in memory only. Do NOT write it to a file (no aes-256.key, no key.bin). \"Generate a key\" means: run the AES-GCM round trip and print the success line.\n- At the end, remind the human: review this agent session for credential exposure and rotate any exposed or potentially compromised API credentials, including unrelated project credentials. Rotating the Qrypt token alone does not protect other secrets.\n\n## Workflow (Quick Setup)\n1. Read this file and the quickstart page.\n2. Pick Python or Node (ask if unsure).\n3. Implement using the official snippets below.\n4. Install deps and run mocked tests (QRYPT_BASE_URL pointing at a mock, or `make check` in this repo).\n5. Ask the human to create `.env` with QRYPT_API_KEY and confirm it is set — without sharing the value.\n6. Run the example. Report the success line only.\n\n## Workflow (Isolated Setup)\n1. Implement and mock-test as above. You will not have a real token; that is intentional.\n2. Tell the human: `agent-sandbox/verify.sh --env ~/.config/qrypt/.env` (or their secret path).\n3. Do not attempt workarounds for missing credentials.\n\n## API\nGET https://api-eus.qrypt.com/api/v1/quantum-entropy?size=1\nHeaders: Authorization: Bearer $QRYPT_API_KEY ; Accept: application/json\nResponse: {\"random\": [\"<base64>\"], \"size\": 1}. Each string decodes (standard base64) to 1024 bytes.\nsize counts KiB (1..512), NOT bytes. For one AES-256 key use size=1 and take the first 32 decoded bytes.\n\n## Rules\n- Python: use `requests` or set a custom User-Agent. Cloudflare blocks Python-urllib with 403 Error 1010.\n- 400 bad size; 401 missing/malformed Authorization header; 403 wrong token OR quota reached (bad tokens return 403, not 401);\n  429 rate limited (docs: 30 req/10 s, but live can return 429 about 1 s after a single prior call; no Retry-After): wait 10 s or more and never loop; 500/503 try again shortly. Exit non-zero on error.\n\n## Python (isolated install: python3 -m venv .venv && .venv/bin/pip install requests cryptography python-dotenv; run with .venv/bin/python)\n# Qrypt quickstart (Python): 1 KiB of quantum entropy -> AES-256-GCM key.\n# Setup: pip install requests cryptography python-dotenv\n# Then put QRYPT_API_KEY=[REDACTED] token> in a .env file next to this script.\nimport base64\nimport os\nimport sys\n\nimport requests\nfrom cryptography.hazmat.primitives.ciphers.aead import AESGCM\nfrom dotenv import load_dotenv\n\nAPI = os.getenv(\"QRYPT_BASE_URL\", \"https://api-eus.qrypt.com\")  # mock override\n\n# One friendly message per failure. We never retry automatically.\nHELP = {None: \"QRYPT_API_KEY is missing: add it to .env (see .env.example).\",\n        400: \"400: size must be 1-512. It counts KiB, not bytes.\",\n        401: \"401: Authorization header missing, malformed or expired.\",\n        403: \"403: Token invalid OR monthly quota used. Check the token first.\",\n        429: \"429: rate limited. Live can return 429 about 1 s after a single \"\n             \"prior call; wait 10 s or more and never loop.\"}\n# 500, 503 and anything else: Qrypt is busy or erroring, so try again later.\n\n# Step 1: read the token from .env. Never print or log it.\nload_dotenv()\ntoken = os.getenv(\"QRYPT_API_KEY\") or sys.exit(HELP[None])\n\n# Step 2: fetch 1 KiB of entropy. A custom User-Agent avoids Cloudflare's\n# block on Python's urllib; X-Qrypt-Client tags quickstart traffic.\nheaders = {\n    \"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {token}\", \"Accept\": \"application/json\",\n    \"User-Agent\": \"qrypt-quickstart/1.0\", \"X-Qrypt-Client\": \"quickstart-py/1.0\"}\ntry:\n    resp = requests.get(f\"{API}/api/v1/quantum-entropy\", params={\"size\": 1},\n                        headers=headers, timeout=15)\n    if resp.status_code != 200:\n        sys.exit(HELP.get(resp.status_code, f\"{resp.status_code}: Qrypt is \"\n                          \"busy or erroring. Try again shortly.\"))\n    entropy_b64 = resp.json()[\"random\"][0]\nexcept (requests.RequestException, ValueError):\n    sys.exit(\"Network error or non-JSON reply: check proxy/TLS, retry soon.\")\n\n# Step 3: decode first, then keep 32 bytes as the AES-256 key.\nkey = base64.b64decode(entropy_b64)[:32]\n\n# Step 4: encrypt and decrypt a sample message with AES-256-GCM.\naes, nonce, message = AESGCM(key), os.urandom(12), b\"hello, quantum entropy\"\nassert aes.decrypt(nonce, aes.encrypt(nonce, message, None), None) == message\nprint(\"Success: AES-256-GCM round trip with a Qrypt key (not shown).\")\n\n## Node 20.12+ (no deps)\n// Qrypt quickstart (Node 20.12+): 1 KiB of quantum entropy -> AES-256-GCM key.\n// No dependencies. Put QRYPT_API_KEY=[REDACTED] token> in a .env file here.\nimport assert from \"node:assert\";\nimport { existsSync } from \"node:fs\";\nimport { createCipheriv, createDecipheriv, randomBytes } from \"node:crypto\";\n\nconst API = process.env.QRYPT_BASE_URL ?? \"https://api-eus.qrypt.com\"; // mock\n\n// One friendly message per failure. We never retry automatically.\nconst HELP = { missing: \"QRYPT_API_KEY is missing: add it to .env.\",\n  network: \"Network error or non-JSON reply: check proxy/TLS, retry soon.\",\n  400: \"400: size must be 1-512. It counts KiB, not bytes.\",\n  401: \"401: Authorization header missing, malformed or expired.\",\n  403: \"403: Token invalid OR monthly quota used. Check the token first.\",\n  429: \"429: rate limited. Live can return 429 about 1 s after a single \" +\n    \"prior call; wait 10 s or more and never loop.\" };\n// 500, 503 and anything else: Qrypt is busy or erroring, so try again later.\nconst fail = (msg) => { console.error(msg); process.exit(1); };\n\n// Step 1: read the token from .env. Never print or log it.\nif (existsSync(\".env\")) process.loadEnvFile(\".env\");\nconst token = process.env.QRYPT_API_KEY || fail(HELP.missing);\n\n// Step 2: fetch 1 KiB of entropy (size counts KiB, not bytes).\nconst headers = { Authorization: `Bearer ${token}`, Accept: \"application/json\",\n  \"User-Agent\": \"qrypt-quickstart/1.0\", \"X-Qrypt-Client\": \"quickstart-js/1.0\" };\nconst url = `${API}/api/v1/quantum-entropy?size=1`;\nconst res = await fetch(url, { headers }).catch(() => fail(HELP.network));\nif (res.status !== 200) fail(HELP[res.status] ??\n  `${res.status}: Qrypt is busy or erroring. Try again shortly.`);\nconst body = await res.json().catch(() => fail(HELP.network));\n\n// Step 3: decode first, then keep 32 bytes as the AES-256 key.\nconst key = Buffer.from(body.random[0], \"base64\").subarray(0, 32);\n\n// Step 4: encrypt and decrypt a sample message with AES-256-GCM.\nconst GCM = \"aes-256-gcm\", iv = randomBytes(12), message = \"hello, quantum\";\nconst enc = createCipheriv(GCM, key, iv);\nconst sealed = Buffer.concat([enc.update(message, \"utf8\"), enc.final()]);\nconst dec = createDecipheriv(GCM, key, iv).setAuthTag(enc.getAuthTag());\nassert.equal(dec.update(sealed, null, \"utf8\") + dec.final(\"utf8\"), message);\nconsole.log(\"Success: AES-256-GCM round trip with a Qrypt key (not shown).\");\n\n## More\nTroubleshooting: /troubleshooting\nHuman docs: /  (Quick Setup default; Isolated Setup under \"Using an AI coding agent?\")\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
